screens-settings-gitlab = GitLab
screens-settings-global-git-config-profile-per-organization = Your global git config, and a profile per organization — the author, the SSH key and the account its repositories use — plus the default branch, how Pull moves a branch, the merge strategy, whether a merged branch is deleted on the code host, the fetch interval, and what the history panel shows.
screens-settings-goals = Goals
screens-settings-governance = Governance
screens-settings-guard = Guard
screens-settings-harnesses = Harnesses
screens-settings-how-checkout-backed-what-follows-merged = How a checkout is backed, what follows a merged pull request, when a checkout is cleaned up, how a dirty one is closed, and how long a workstream script may run. The scripts themselves are written per project in About › Settings, which also approves them on this machine.
screens-settings-how-designer-behaves-machine-snapping-grid = How the designer behaves on this machine — snapping, the grid, the minimap — how long it waits before saving a revision, and how many finished runs in the workspace each workflow keeps.
screens-settings-how-much-scratchpad-screen-how-behaves = How much of the scratchpad is on screen, and how it behaves while you write. All of it is window state on this machine — a note never leaves it.
screens-settings-how-new-goal-moves-auto-guided = How a new goal moves — auto, guided or manual — and how many failed runs an auto goal repairs on its own before it asks.
screens-settings-identity = Identity
screens-settings-key-each-organization-generate-here-put = A key for each organization: generate it here, put its public half on the host, check that the host knows it, then bind it in a profile — one card per key, one step at a time. Public material only: nothing here opens a private key or writes your ssh config.
screens-settings-keymap = Keymap
screens-settings-keypair-account-there-no-server-knows = The keypair is the account: there is no server that knows you and no reset link, so where it lives is the thing worth knowing.
screens-settings-keys-tokens-values-rules-recognise-never = Keys, tokens and values the rules recognise never reach an agent or a harness: they travel as placeholders, and are restored only where a command is about to run on this machine.
screens-settings-language-servers = Language servers
screens-settings-library = Library
screens-settings-logging = Logging
