screens-settings-teams-workspace-can-install-installing-one = The teams a workspace can install; installing one brings its agents.
screens-settings-terminal = Terminal
screens-settings-tool-commands-guard-every-command-path = The Tool & Commands Guard: every command, path and tool an agent asks its harness to run is judged first — allowed, refused with the reason, put to you in the Inbox, or read by the classifier. Rules are tried in order; the first match decides.
screens-settings-tools-agent-may-given-registered-machine = Tools an agent may be given. Registered on this machine and never synced — what travels is the id.
screens-settings-what-agents-read-from-outside-page = What agents read from outside: a page opened with the platform's browser and a review read from a code host are put to the classifier before the agent reads them — safe passes framed as data; harmful, or no verdict, holds the content and asks you where the agent works, with the source, the reason and an excerpt. A harness's own fetch and web search cannot be screened, so the guard asks before them and points the agent at the browser tools.
screens-settings-what-mac-lets-desktop-app-do = What this Mac lets the desktop app do — which notifications reach you, by what happened; Full Disk Access and, for voice mode later, the microphone, both off until you turn them on. The permissions themselves are macOS's to give.
screens-settings-what-mac-s-network-whether-internet = What this Mac's network is — whether the internet is reachable and by which public IP, every interface that is up, the VPN and its tunnel, the route and the resolvers, the proxy System Settings names, read and never changed — and how the platform reaches the internet: the proxy it and everything it runs follow, and whether it speaks HTTP/1.1 only.
screens-settings-what-node-desktop-write-about-themselves = What the node and the desktop write about themselves, on this machine: errors by default, more when asked.
screens-settings-what-page-agent-made-may-reach = What a page an agent made may reach: libraries from three public CDNs, or nothing beyond what it carries.
screens-settings-what-platform-s-own-calls-may = What the platform's own calls may reach: a connector step or an account check is refused before it leaves when its host is on the deny list, and beyond what the connector declares only when it is on the allow list. One host per line; a leading dot covers subdomains.
screens-settings-where-tools-machine-when-search-above = Where the tools are on this machine, when the search above does not find them.
screens-settings-whether-mac-signed-bitbucket-accounts-platform = Whether this Mac is signed in to Bitbucket — the accounts this platform holds an API token for and git's own credential helper — who pull requests go as, and a way in: an API token beside its login, since Bitbucket Cloud has no CLI of its own.
screens-settings-whether-mac-signed-github-github-cli = Whether this Mac is signed in to GitHub — the GitHub CLI, the accounts this platform holds a token for, git's own credential helper — who pull requests go as, and a way in: the CLI's browser sign-in, or a token.
screens-settings-whether-mac-signed-gitlab-gitlab-cli = Whether this Mac is signed in to GitLab — the GitLab CLI, the accounts this platform holds a token for, git's own credential helper — who merge requests go as, and a way in: the CLI's browser sign-in, or a token.
screens-settings-whether-servers-run-which-ones-machine = Whether servers run, which ones this machine has, and how long an idle one is kept.
